    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d284">

                <pb facs="0341" n="241" xml:id="pg241"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">412.00/125: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-09-13T12:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">September 13,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 5:25 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>392. The local press today publishes an Executive decree amending article 15 of
                    the Executive decree August 30, 1919 regarding claims<anchor n="67"
                        xml:id="d284-f1"/> (Embassy’s despatch number 2406 of September 17,
                        1919<anchor n="68" xml:id="d284-f2"/>) so as to admit claims for damages
                    caused up to June 30th 1920 and to extend until February 5th 1921 the period in
                    which such claims may be presented.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
